"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including the preoperative PSA of 4.7 and the pathological T-stage of pT3a with extraprostatic extension. Positive surgical margins are also a noted concern. Countervailing findings include no seminal vesicle invasion and an absence of lymphovascular invasion. The lack of nodal sampling widens uncertainty regarding nodal status. Biopsy results showed Gleason 3+3 (ISUP grade group 1) in the peripheral zone, which differs from the prostatectomy specimen's Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2). Prognostic revision would be significantly aided by postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent trajectory. The current data is limited by missing nodal sampling information. The fixed estimated horizon is 62.79 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 40.81–84.77 months; its coverage has not been validated."
